Which of the following is a common component of a Command and Control (C2) infrastructure? > C2 server, C2 agent, C2 communication channel

When using a C2 framework, which of the following protocols would likely raise the least suspicion when used as a communication channel? > HTTP

Which of the following is a common technique used by C2 frameworks to maintain persistence on compromised systems? > Creating a service that restarts automatically after rebooting.

DNS also can be used in C2 communication channel by allowing data to be embedded in DNS queries or responses.

Which of the following techniques is often used by C2 frameworks to avoid detection by Intrusion Detection Systems (IDS)? > Obfuscation of C2 traffic to resemble normal network traffic.

A centralized C2 framework has a single point of failure. What is a common mitigation strategy for this vulnerability? > Using redundant C2 servers with automatic failover.

Which of the following best describes "command chaining" in C2 frameworks? > Executing multiple commands in sequence to automate tasks.

What is a key consideration when choosing a location to deploy a C2 server for red teaming? >

1.The server should be placed in a highly secure environment to prevent unauthorized access.
2.The deployment location should not raise suspicion, often mimicking typical server environments.
3.The server should be hosted in a location with low latency to ensure fast communication with agents

A C2 framework may use Domain Fronting as an evasion technique. What does Domain Fronting involve? > Redirecting C2 traffic through well-known domains to evade detection.

The C2 Framework "Covenant" supports Linux and macOS payloads. > False

What is the role of a kill switch in a C2 framework during a red team exercise? > To terminate C2 operations if the exercise is compromised or needs to end.

Which of the following open source C2 frameworks supports deploying agents and payloads on Windows systems? > Empire, Covenant, Metasploit
